{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And he encountered the place.</b> It happened to him that he reached a place he had not intended. What is meant by \"the place\" is a lodging place for travelers, which was then prepared in every city, usually in the city square. Concerning this, the angels said to Lot (Genesis 19:2): כִּי בָרְחוֹב נָלִין, and likewise regarding the concubine in Gibeah (Judges 19:20): רַק בָּרְחוֹב אַל תָּלַן." "<b>From the stones of the place.</b> Which were kept there for travelers — to eat upon and to sit upon."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:09.015400492Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}